# IPC & Preload

- Register ALL IPC handlers inside the single `registerIpcHandlers` function in `apps/desktop/src/ipc/ipc.ts`.
- The preload (`apps/desktop/src/preload/preload.ts`) exposes a typed `window.electronAPI` via `contextBridge`. Only whitelisted methods are exposed. Never expose `ipcRenderer` or Node globals directly.
- Channel names follow the `domain:action` pattern: `weight:update`, `serial:status`, `settings:get-all`, `records:create`.

## Request-response

Use `ipcMain.handle` / `ipcRenderer.invoke`.

```ts
// ipc.ts
ipcMain.handle('records:create', (_e, data) => { /* ... */ });
// preload.ts
createRecord: (data) => ipcRenderer.invoke('records:create', data),
```

## Streaming (e.g. weight updates)

Main sends via `mainWindow.webContents.send()`; the preload wraps the listener and returns an unsubscribe function.

```ts
onWeightUpdate: (cb) => {
  const handler = (_e, reading) => cb(reading);
  ipcRenderer.on('weight:update', handler);
  return () => ipcRenderer.removeListener('weight:update', handler);
},
```
